          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18502 ptlrpc: print enable_cap_mask as a YAML flow mapping",
        "message": "LU-18502 ptlrpc: print enable_cap_mask as a YAML flow mapping\n\nWhen the cap type is not \"off\", nodemap.*.enable_cap_mask prints\n\"type: ...\" and \"caps: ...\" on two lines. \"lctl get_param --yaml\"\nputs the first line on the line of the key. A YAML parser rejects\nthis output.\n\nPrint the type and the caps as one YAML flow mapping on one line.\nThe other nodemap parameters also use the flow style. Quote the\ncaps, because a comma ends a plain value in a flow mapping.\n\ncfs_mask2str() no longer adds a newline. Its callers add the newline,\nso the output of the other callers does not change.\n\nIn sanity-sec test_25c, set a cap mask on the nodemap and check the\nexact value.\n\nFixes: 5768bf35fd74 (\"LU-18502 utils: Support YAML for get_param parameter names\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=25c\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5\nChange-Id: I582ee0634a8af5b71eb86d39b64f930b4df47730\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
